{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787994135260,"sessionID":"ses_fb3458985ffeeMJ5OFBVh1MOcx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_75349b3a1cb24582a325fb6a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","limit":28,"offset":588},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n588:   - `POST /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/push` — `git push -u origin <branch>`\n589:     (mirroring the TUI git panel's push), bounded by a 30s timeout so a\n590:     stalled remote can't hang the request; a failure surfaces as a structured\n591:     error with git's own message.\n592:   - `POST /prune` — prune orphaned manigot-* containers\n593:     (`session.PruneOrphans`), deliberately top-level (not under a project):\n594:     containers are not partitioned by project. Reports removed + running\n595:     counts.\n596:   - `GET /projects/<p>/orphans` — list the project's orphaned worktrees\n597:     (`job.DiscoverOrphans`), read-only.\n598:   - `POST /projects/<p>/orphans/<name>/delete` — remove one named orphan\n599:     (`job.MatchOrphan` then `job.RemoveOrphansConfirmed`), the HTTP call\n600:     itself the confirmation. One named resource per call, never a\n601:     delete-everything route.\n602: - **Live run supervision.** `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/session-log/stream` —\n603:   Server-Sent Events over the plain `net/http` server (no WebSocket upgrade,\n604:   no new dependency): the network twin of the TUI's `l` key, tailing the same\n605:   `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` the TUI tails locally. It starts at the\n606:   file's current size (tail -f — only new growth), at byte 0 when the file\n607:   doesn't exist yet (the launch-then-watch flow), or at `?from=<byte offset>`\n608:   (the reconnect contract — a client resumes where it dropped and loses\n609:   nothing); a truncated file resets to byte 0 with a fresh `start` event. Each\n610:   new line is flushed as an SSE `data:` frame, with a keepalive comment on\n611:   idle. The stream stops on client disconnect **and** participates in the\n612:   daemon's graceful shutdown: `Server.Shutdown` cancels a server-scoped\n613:   context before draining, so an open stream unblocks and the drain returns\n614:   promptly instead of waiting out its full timeout.\n615: - **Binding + auth.** Binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default, tokenless — the\n\n(Showing lines 588-615 of 848. Use offset=616 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"  - `POST /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/push` — `git push -u origin <branch>`\n    (mirroring the TUI git panel's push), bounded by a 30s timeout so a\n    stalled remote can't hang the request; a failure surfaces as a structured\n    error with git's own message.\n  - `POST /prune` — prune orphaned manigot-* containers\n    (`session.PruneOrphans`), deliberately top-level (not under a project):\n    containers are not partitioned by project. Reports removed + running\n    counts.\n  - `GET /projects/<p>/orphans` — list the project's orphaned worktrees\n    (`job.DiscoverOrphans`), read-only.\n  - `POST /projects/<p>/orphans/<name>/delete` — remove one named orphan\n    (`job.MatchOrphan` then `job.RemoveOrphansConfirmed`), the HTTP call\n    itself the confirmation. One named resource per call, never a\n    delete-everything route.\n- **Live run supervision.** `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/session-log/stream` —\n  Server-Sent Events over the plain `net/http` server (no WebSocket upgrade,\n  no new dependency): the network twin of the TUI's `l` key, tailing the same\n  `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` the TUI tails locally. It starts at the\n  file's current size (tail -f — only new growth), at byte 0 when the file\n  doesn't exist yet (the launch-then-watch flow), or at `?from=<byte offset>`","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"  - `POST /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/push` — `git push -u origin <branch>`\n    (mirroring the TUI git panel's push), bounded by a 30s timeout so a\n    stalled remote can't hang the request; a failure surfaces as a structured\n    error with git's own message.\n  - `POST /prune` — prune orphaned manigot-* containers\n    (`session.PruneOrphans`), deliberately top-level (not under a project):\n    containers are not partitioned by project. Reports removed + running\n    counts.\n  - `GET /projects/<p>/orphans` — list the project's orphaned worktrees\n    (`job.DiscoverOrphans`), read-only.\n  - `POST /projects/<p>/orphans/<name>/delete` — remove one named orphan\n    (`job.MatchOrphan` then `job.RemoveOrphansConfirmed`), the HTTP call\n    itself the confirmation. One named resource per call, never a\n    delete-everything route.\n- **Live run supervision.** `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/session-log/stream` —\n  Server-Sent Events over the plain `net/http` server (no WebSocket upgrade,\n  no new dependency): the network twin of the TUI's `l` key, tailing the same\n  `docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log` the TUI tails locally. It starts at the\n  file's current size (tail -f — only new growth), at byte 0 when the file\n  doesn't exist yet (the launch-then-watch flow), or at `?from=<byte offset>`\n  (the reconnect contract — a client resumes where it dropped and loses\n  nothing); a truncated file resets to byte 0 with a fresh `start` event. Each\n  new line is flushed as an SSE `data:` frame, with a keepalive comment on\n  idle. The stream stops on client disconnect **and** participates in the\n  daemon's graceful shutdown: `Server.Shutdown` cancels a server-scoped\n  context before draining, so an open stream unblocks and the drain returns\n  promptly instead of waiting out its full timeout.\n- **Binding + auth.** Binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default, tokenless — the","lineStart":588,"lineEnd":615,"totalLines":848,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787994135229,"end":1787994135251}},"id":"prt_04cc15ab5001EIWupGq9sHw2Z1","sessionID":"ses_fb3458985ffeeMJ5OFBVh1MOcx",