s add/rm` — or by editing — and restart), so\n-any surface — a web UI, a\n+changing it means editing and restarting), so any surface — a web UI, a\n native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client from localhost or a\n VPS. It binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default (tokenless —\n the machine's own user is the trust boundary); a non-loopback bind REQUIRES a\n=== merge-base version ===\n113:TUI's settings screen) — see the manigot README's Theme section. This is a\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && git diff main..HEAD -- project-template/docs/AGENTS.md; echo \"=== merge-base version ===\"; git show 376aca2:project-template/docs/AGENTS.md | grep -n \"settings\\|serve-projects\" | head","time":{"start":1787994842853,"end":1787994842855}},"id":"prt_04ccc25d2001lL5KlERhQNwPQB","sessionID":"ses_fb3368eedffetvzxol071th185","messageID":"msg_04ccbf9bd001spOJLq77tSX85f"}}
