{"type":"text","timestamp":1787994864160,"sessionID":"ses_fb3368eedffetvzxol071th185","part":{"id":"prt_04ccc6e1c001KCNL2zaQDu6KT7","messageID":"msg_04ccc6183001mBckYiAdLhpxbq","sessionID":"ses_fb3368eedffetvzxol071th185","type":"text","text":"Job work complete. Summary:\n\n**State found:** The prior developer session had already implemented and committed the full feature (`164a363`) but was interrupted before writing `implementation.md` — it remained a template. The implementation was sound: `GET/PUT /settings` (default profile via `config.UpsertEnv`, the shared `mg profiles` write path), `GET/PUT /projects/{project}/settings` (baseBranch + jobBranchPrefix via `project.Save`, ref-component validated, project-locked), plus test surface pins and docs.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...` pass\n- All affected packages (`internal/serve`, `internal/config`, `internal/project`) pass\n- Full-suite failures are confined to packages needing `git init`/`git worktree`, blocked by the container's git shim — 284 shim refusals, zero non-shim causes, unrelated to this change\n\n**Done now:** Wrote `docs/jobs/brother_api-routes-for-settings/implementation.md` (TASK-1..4 coverage, changes, verification) and committed as `19b0716`.\n\nNote: the branch is one commit behind main (`0ff5d7d mg serve config via cli`); both sides edited `docs/AGENTS.md` in disjoint regions, so `mg done`'s squash merge should resolve cleanly. `verdict.md` is the reviewer's deliverable.","time":{"start":1787994861084,"end":1787994864157}}}
